# Nothing in this repository is line-ending-converted on checkout or on commit.
#
# Almost everything here that is a test is a BYTE comparison: `tests/fixtures/planes/**` are
# copied into every recorded scenario, `tests/fixtures/recorded/` compares every file a command
# leaves and every byte it prints against the recorded answer (ADR 0046),
# `fixtures/corpora/*.raw` are raw terminal recordings with escape sequences in them, and a good
# part of `crates/charter-core` asserts on exact output. Git for Windows enables `core.autocrlf` by default, and a checkout that rewrote a
# line ending would make every one of those tests measure the checkout instead of the code —
# silently, and only on one platform.
#
# `-text` and not `text=auto`: `auto` still normalises on the way IN, which is a rewrite of a
# recording nobody asked for. This repository's files are LF and stay LF everywhere.
* -text
